verdict.failing_test_idea:
Two tests at the person's boundary.

UI: apps/ui/test/project.test.tsx. In the fake daemon, a project with 3 done tasks (progress.total 3) gets intake state 'pending' (an Add to plan). Render /projects/:id/summary and expect screen.getAllByText(/Waiting for you: approve the plan/) to have length 1, with one Open link to /inbox. Today it has length 2: data-testid project-status and intake-banner.

Runtime: a composed or real-daemon test. Approve an intake whose first session holds 3 tasks, where tasks 2 and 3 depend on task 1, then start. Read GET /sessions/:id/events with details:
- the size is stated once, or the Plan line's count equals the promise's (no 'Plan: 1 task' beside 'It promised 3 tasks');
- the first-session summary does not say "1 task" when 3 were approved;
- no line reads 'note for the next session' for a note this session consumed.

packages/runtime/test/chat-recall.test.ts, or a real-daemon case in apps/ui/test/real-daemon.test.ts through POST /chat/stream (streamChat), with a scripted provider. Ask "what did I say about the pizza oven?". Step 1 answers "I can't find anything about a pizza oven in Quote Page's tasks... I haven't searched the records yet. Should I look?" with no tool call; step 2 calls recall {words:"pizza oven"}; step 3 answers from the result. Assert that:
- the person's reply contains the recall result's "Looked through:" wording and not "Should I look";
- recall ran once and model calls are at most 6;
- the streamed bubble never ends on the offer.
Today the turn ends after step 1 and shows the offer, so the test fails. Add a paid tests/live case on claude-haiku-5-5 at effort low: a Quote Page conversation seeded with 3 earlier "Should I look...?" replies, then the two control lines. Each turn must call recall and reply without guessing another project.

verdict.fix_sketch:
Keep the reply's line structure in inAppText. Collapse only runs of spaces and tabs (/[^\S
]{2,}/g -> " "), drop spaces at the end of each line, collapse three or more newlines to "

", and trim. Another option is a separate inAppReply for model text that removes only the voice and email hints and skips the whitespace collapse, used at Conversation.tsx:560 and kept the same as the live bubble at :342. The read-backs and card lines that use inAppText today are single-line, so they are unaffected. Optional: in RichText, keep one line break between a list and the text after it, so a blank line after a list still shows as a gap. That part is cosmetic: the list already ends correctly.

Put one figure for "the waiting work" in start-check.ts, for example waitingWorkUsdMicro(check, inFlight). It would add up:
- promiseOf(check).estimateUsdMicro (runnable + the larger task's room + later followers);
- the claimed or in_progress tasks, priced as the planner prices them: planEstimateUsdMicro(estimates, t, keptWorkFor(...)) minus what the task has spent in total (work plus reviews), floored at 0;
- the whole sum capped at the work budget.
Use it in three places:
1. the compose.ts ask closure, in place of the runnable + raw-est sum;
2. server.ts credentialAtStart, in place of runnable only, so the dialog's "Use API key ... about CHF N" counts the followers the session would take;
3. the plan card's foot line under a stop, so it is the same figure when the plan's tasks are what waits.
That closes C6L-3's "one figure per thing" as well. Update credential-ask-figure.test.ts: it now pins "the task's own estimate" (the raw est). Leave the words "for what waits now" as they are: the agent's added tasks are outside the estimate by design.

